P/U weight at 3300 m was 6150 lbs.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T01:10:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T01:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3310</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Had to pull back up and RIH again. Was able to pass on second attempt. Continued to RIH.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T01:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T02:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3620</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>RIH with tractor from 3310 to 3620 m. WHP 93,3 bar.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T02:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T03:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3570</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Correlated in short pup joint from 3582,9 to 3588,9 m. Adjusted depth by 3,4 m. Continued to RIH with tractor from 3570 to 3790 m to perform first correlation pass.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T03:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T03:50:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3570</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Correlated across perforation depth from 3790 to 3570 m, and verified correct depth. P/U weight was 8400 lbs when picking up from 3790 m. Observed much noise on the CCL, made it challeng to read clear CCL signals.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T03:50:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T05:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3700</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>RIH with tractor to perform correlation pass across perforating interval from 3790 to 3700 m. Observed the joints in the perforating area was 1 meter off. RIH again and performed a new correlation pass. The joints was within 0,5 m tolerance.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T05:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T06:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">3724.6</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Performed final correlation. Performed final up pass and placed top shot at 3715 and bottom shot at 3724,6. Lined up for firing guns through Altus safe sub.
Perforated interval 3715 - 3724,6 m. WHP 95,5 bar. Observed 250 lbs. drop in tension, and approx. 2 bar drop on DHPG. Pulled slowly out of hole after perforation.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T06:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T08:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>POOH w/BHA #4 tractor and short perforation gun from 3700m to surface.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T08:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T09:50:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>OOH, closed SV and HMV. Inflow tested same. Flushed RU with N2. SIWHP 96 bar.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T09:50:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T10:05:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Held brief before LD BHA and perforating guns.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T10:05:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T10:45:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Lifted lubricator and LD BHA #4 tractor and short perforation gun. All shots fired.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2014-12-04T10:45:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2014-12-04T11:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- perforate</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>BHA on deck. Closed BOP and prepared for flowing well for cleanup. 
